A||N||6||beachbomb||Spark plug wire question||||5||
Z||000000||beachbomb||05-15-2001||04:49 PM||||Hi all, is there anywhere i can get a good set of plug wires for my 4 cyclinder fiero indy, i bought a pair from Pep Boys, but after a month the part that hooks to the plug iteself couldn't take the heat and got real soft and eventually caused a short,,,any suggestions, please help..thanks.<BR>p.s. i noticed the original wires had real thick rubber by the plugs, i'm trying to find some like that..thanks..Jim(2 '84 Indys)||||reg||5
Z||000001||johnt671||05-15-2001||06:26 PM||||I went to a local parts store and found a nice set of 8mm Accel wires made for a 4 cyl for (if I recall right)around $25.  Maybe check to be sure your wires are out of the way of the rising heat and behind the heat shield as much as possible.  I melted the first set I put on mine too.||||reg||1
Z||000002||beachbomb||05-15-2001||06:33 PM||||Thanks, i'll keep looking around here, i have them hoocked up to the proper hooks, just seemed to melt right where the heat sheild is at, where the wire comes closest to the engine,,thanks..Jim||||reg||1
Z||000003||rogergarrison||05-15-2001||07:35 PM||||make sure you use the metal protectors from your old wires on the new ones if they dont have them.||||reg||1
Z||000004||beachbomb||05-15-2001||08:03 PM||||Mine didn't have metal protectors on them old or new, where can i get them at, also where on the wires do they go..thanks..jim||||reg||1
Z||000005||RacinRob||05-16-2001||02:16 AM||||I Have a universal set of 8mm accel wires and they do the job, without the metal heat shield. I bought a v-8 set for like 25 bucks and did them up myself, it's not hard, and than you have a few extra wires.||||reg||1
Z||000006||DXR_DAD||05-16-2001||02:55 AM||||I've got the Accel 300+ 8.8mm universal, about $60.00 a set. I have had no problems at all!!! they still wook and feel like new and no metal protectors on the boot<BR>The best thing is you can custom fit them,<P>DXR_DAD||||reg||14
